    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "837beecf-4239-4b3d-b683-1d611af3da2e",
      "key": "3e565573-7ef6-4c28-95e5-295fb152be76",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureTitle",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Itinerary"
        },
        {
          "alias": "richTextContent",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Ch3\u003EDay 1\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EWe depart by private executive coach from our designated pick up points. En route to our hotel we visit the National Trust\u2019s Attingham Park in Shropshire, an elegant 18th century mansion, and home to a fine collection of ambassadorial silver, Italian furniture and Grand Tour paintings. We continue to the 4* Albrighton Hall Hotel and Spa where we stay four nights on a half board basis.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EDay 2\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EWith our Blue Badge guide we enjoy a full day at Ironbridge Gorge. The great symbol of the success of the iron industry can be found at the heart of the small town that bears its name. Cast in 1779 by Abraham Darby the 3rd, its great arch enthralled visitors who came from all over the world to admire its construction, as they still do today. With our guide, we see the Ironbridge and Toll House, and visit the Coalport China Museum. The afternoon is at leisure to explore the Blists Hill Victorian Village. The Museum is a recreation of life in a Victorian community. Working factories, shops and cottages are authentic to the era, as are the \u2018townsfolk\u2019.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EDay 3\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EWith our Blue Badge guide this morning we visit the English Heritage\u2019s Stokesay Castle. Nestling in a green valley in the heart of the Shropshire countryside, this perfectly preserved medieval fortified manor house dates back to the 11th century. After spending some time at leisure in Ludlow for lunch, we continue to Kidderminster. On arrival, we enjoy an included one way 16 mile steam train excursion to Bridgnorth on the Severn Valley Railway, the best way to explore the beauty of the River Severn. We spend the rest of the day at leisure at the historic town of Bridgnorth, once a thriving port along the banks of the River Severn. Upon seeing Bridgnorth, Charles the First declared the destination as offering \u2018the finest view in all my Kingdom\u2019, as he gazed, awestruck, from the top of this delightful town.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EDay 4\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EOur guided walking tour of Shrewsbury this morning takes in sights such as the Norman Castle and St Mary\u2019s Church, dating from 960 AD and boasting one of the tallest spires in England. The rest of the day is at leisure to explore Shrewsbury, famous for its breezy black and white \u2018magpie\u2019 houses so typical of the Welsh Marches. On an individual basis you may choose to visit Shrewsbury Prison, or enjoy a cruise on the River Severn.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EDay 5\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EToday we enjoy a guided tour of the Wedgwood Factory where we see craftsmen at work, utilising unique artisan skills and techniques homed over 250 years at Barlaston. The visit offers an in depth view of all aspects of quality ceramic production including casting, figure making, pattern decorating and hand painting, ornamentation and gilding. Time is then at leisure at the attraction, and you may choose to explore the V\u0026amp;A Wedgwood Collection. Designs and wares saved by the factory and Wedgwood family grew into one of the most important industrial collections in the world. Comprising over 175,000 works of art, ceramics, manuscripts and photographs, the V\u0026amp;A Wedgwood Collection documents production up to the present day, showcasing innovations in taste and fashion spanning over 260 years. Taking carefully selected comfort stops en route, we return back to our original pick up points.\u003C/p\u003E\n"
          }
        },
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureDescription",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": ""
        },
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureSummary",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003ENB:- Please note we reserve the right to alter the above itinerary if required for operational\nreasons. Given the historic nature of the places visited, there will be a large amount of walking, some slopes to climb and some uneven surfaces to negotiate. Participants must also be able to get on and off the coach unaided. As a result, this holiday may not be suitable for those with mobility problems.\u003C/p\u003E\n"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
